      "answer": "ANSWER: In the 2022\u201111\u201128 version of the **Create a release** endpoint there was no `make_latest` field. Whether a release appeared as the repository\u2019s \u201cLatest\u201d release was decided by an internal, undocumented heuristic that looked only at the release\u2019s publish date together with its `draft` and `prerelease` flags. This heuristic could incorrectly mark an older, already\u2011published release as \u201cLatest\u201d if a newer release was still a draft or prerelease.\n\nStarting with API version **2025\u201106\u201101**, the endpoint adds a new `make_latest` parameter (type\u202fenum, default\u202f`true`). The possible values are:\n\n| Value   | Meaning |\n|---------|---------|\n| `true`  | Explicitly mark this release as the repository\u2019s \u201cLatest\u201d release. |\n| `false` | Do **not** mark this release as \u201cLatest\u201d (the repository\u2019s existing latest release remains unchanged). |\n| `legacy`| Preserve the old behavior (use the internal heuristic). |\n\nBy providing `make_latest`, callers now have explicit, documented control over the \u201cLatest\u201d status instead of relying on the previous hidden heuristic. This replaces the undocumented logic with a clear, API\u2011driven option.",
